{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_18","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"python3 - <<'PY'\nimport json, hashlib\nfrom pathlib import Path\nr=json.load(open('runtime_context.json'))\nids=r['context']['allowed_observation_ids']\nvariants=[]\nfor mass,query in [(True,True),(False,True),(True,False),(False,False)]:\n name=f'mass_m{int(mass)}_q{int(query)}'\n file='candidate.py' if mass and query else name+'.py'\n config={'embedding_dim':16,'token_dim':32,'refresh_query':query,'mass_scaling':mass}\n sha=hashlib.sha256(Path(file).read_bytes()).hexdigest()\n variants.append(dict(name=name,file=file,role='candidate' if mass and query else 'control',config=config,note=f'Prospective factorial cell M={int(mass)}, Q={int(query)}. Explicit log-count in every cell; history-conditioned write always enabled. Source SHA256 {sha}. Host reproduction: instantiate this standalone Model with this config under protocol {r[\\\"required_study_protocol_ref\\\"]}; default host sum of four BCEs. No outcome measured; syntax/source checks only.'))\nfixed=['16-dimensional sparse embeddings and identical field/token identity','token_dim=32, two field mixers, two strictly masked reads and one history-conditioned write','all four tasks, shared visible inputs, explicit log1p(prefix count)/log(101) in all four towers','identical train seed, data/order, single epoch, batch8192, BF16, optimizers, rates and host validation scorer','identical learned parameter count and initialization order across all four cells']\nstudy={\n'id':'g1-history-mass-query-factorial',\n'protocol_ref':r['required_study_protocol_ref'],\n'evidence_refs':ids,\n'question':'Does count-dependent retrieval magnitude improve the unsuccessful iterative field/history exchange model beyond an explicit history-length feature, and does its effect depend on refreshing queries from retrieved evidence?',\n'hypothesis':'Observation: baseline-din click AUC=0.65554408 exceeds all four exchange cells (0.63229720..0.64745824). With writing enabled, refreshing queries adds 0.00200171 AUC; with refresh enabled, writing adds 0.00671789; their single-seed difference-in-differences is -0.00644144. These are descriptive matched contrasts, not repeated support. The best exchange is worse than DIN in every declared history-length slice, including empty histories, so history pooling cannot explain the whole deficit. Inspected exchange source uses sum-one reads over a 32-dimensional event bottleneck, whereas DIN retains full item/action values and unconstrained local weights. Mechanism hypothesis: averaging away prefix-dependent read magnitude can limit how retrieved evidence changes field states and their next queries. A square-root visible-count multiplier at both reads may restore a useful multiplicative path, beyond providing the count to prediction towers. This is one admissible explanation of failure, not evidence that compression or normalization caused it.',\n'nearest_work':[\n {'source_ref':'paper:din','verification':'read','difference':'Archived primary text arXiv:1706.06978v4 lines272-277 explicitly motivates abandoning softmax normalization to preserve interest intensity. This experiment retains softmax relative weights and multiplies them by sqrt(visible count), rather than using learned unnormalized DIN activation scores; visible count is not target-specific learned interest intensity. It embeds that test in an iterative field/history structure. No DIN reproduction or originality claim.'},\n {'source_ref':'unirank-code:EST','verification':'implementation_checked','difference':'Pinned90bb99a60724e975ec565836266fd86dcad0039d source lines158-282 repeats cross-attention and mixed FFNs with token-specific Q/output projections. We retain the previous shared-projection field/history exchange, strictly mask padded scores, keep its affine feedback write, and test retrieval magnitude x feedback query. Original EST paper detail is unavailable through the authorized archive; novelty relative to it remains unverified.'},\n {'source_ref':'unirank-code:INFNet','verification':'implementation_checked','difference':'Pinned benchmark source lines188-217 alternates hub aggregation and affine broadcast; lines222-249 document mask-free aggregation with zeroed sequence K/V. Our inherited writer is a shared field-mean-conditioned affine residual, with strictly masked reads, no task hubs and no task-mask routing. This follow-up adds only count-dependent read magnitude and a count feature; it does not reproduce INFNet.'}\n],\n'inherited_components':['Entire two-round field-mix/read/write architecture of g1-r0000-exchange_q1_w1, including action-valued histories, visible position scalar, direct raw current-field bypass and four Dice towers','Same read projections, strict score masks and empty-history zero-read behavior; identical field/history widths','Feedback write enabled in all cells; query refresh factor inherited from the prior factorial','Frozen host input contract, train recipe, scoring and default four-task unweighted BCE; no host changes'],\n'proposed_difference':'At each of the two field-to-history reads, multiply masked, renormalized softmax weights by sqrt(n) in M1, or by1 in M0, where n is the number of visible history events. Relative attention weights remain identical before downstream feedback effects. Expose log1p(n)/log(101) to every task tower in every cell. Cross M with second-read query source Q: first_fields (refreshed) vs first_query (static). Both query groups retain the first-read evidence through the second field mixer and writer; Q isolates an additional query path, not all history feedback. This is a mechanism diagnostic continuing an unsuccessful trajectory, not a claimed new model contribution. No compression-width or optimizer change.',\n'predictions':[\n 'Primary predeclared contrast: click AUC(mass_m1_q1) > click AUC(mass_m0_q1), with equal learned capacity and explicit count in both.',\n 'If count-scaled evidence specifically helps query/evidence co-evolution, the M1-M0 click AUC contrast should be larger for Q1 than Q0. A main effect without that interaction supports only a read-magnitude effect, not a query-feedback mechanism.',\n 'Report all four AUC/Logloss values and auxiliary mean separately; click AUC selects. Compare the best new cell with baseline-din as a performance reference; failure to exceed0.65554408 means DIN remains incumbent even if within-family effects improve.',\n 'Reuse predeclared history bins empty,1-16,17-64,>64. Expected benefit should occur with nonempty histories, not be inferred from a changed overall history mix. Report sample/positive/negative counts and mark insufficient bins. Existing validation counts: empty6444/427/6017;1-16:461684/28818/432866;17-64:1001754/55298/946456;>64:1401885/50957/1350928. Training-induced empty-slice differences remain possible; n=0 must give an exact zero read in either mode for fixed parameters.',\n 'Within-cell fixed-parameter host checks: valid attention sum=1 for M0 or sqrt(n) for M1, zero for n=0; n=1 modes coincide, masked-value perturbations do not change predictions, finite outputs/backward for empty/mixed/full prefixes. Collect host parameter/cost/memory/throughput/latency metrics; no efficiency claim from equal pass counts alone.'\n],\n'falsifiers':[\n 'M1Q1 does not beat M0Q1 on full validation click AUC: this square-root count implementation is unsupported under the frozen recipe. Do not call normalization or iterative exchange refuted generally.',\n 'The M effect is no greater at Q1 than Q0: reject evidence for positive coupling to query refresh, even if an overall M gain exists.',\n 'Comparable gain only in normalized-plus-count controls relative to historical cells, with no M advantage: explicit count or changed tower/optimization is sufficient at this resolution; historical comparisons also change initialization shape and cannot isolate count causally.',\n 'Nonfinite host forward/backward, incorrect mask behavior, invalid source/interface or trial-cap overrun invalidates the affected run; retain failed costs and do not interpret execution failures scientifically.',\n 'A future paired-seed reversal or equal-cost disadvantage weakens a provisional one-seed improvement; one run cannot establish a general mechanism.'\n],\n'alternative_explanations':[\n 'The32-dimensional event projection may lose field/action information, and normalized values/field mixers may dominate; this study does not isolate compression.',\n 'Count-dependent scaling may merely improve optimization or residual branch balance in the fixed single-pass, low-dense-learning-rate recipe. Even a positive factorial interaction does not exclude this. A later constant-gain replacement with equal count features is needed before attributing gains specifically to per-user intensity.',\n 'History length correlates with prevalence, user activity and truncation. n counts only the released visible prefix, capped100; it cannot establish long-term preference intensity or production causal validity.',\n 'The explicit count feature adds512 dense weights versus old exchange models and changes tower initialization shape; comparisons with old trials are context, not exact count-only contrasts. Within the four new cells all modules, active capacity and initialization order match.',\n 'Single-seed variation, task sharing, calibration and the inherited offline feedback maturity assumptions can explain apparent gains; no withheld assessment is authorized in this phase.'\n],\n'contrasts':[\n dict(parent_ref='g1-r0000-exchange_q1_w1',intervention='mass_m1_q1: sqrt(n)-scaled masked reads, refreshed second query',control='mass_m0_q1: sum-one masked reads, refreshed second query; same explicit log-count',held_fixed=fixed,remaining_confounds=['Per-user gain changes optimization and subsequent writer conditioning as well as retrieved magnitude','No constant-gain replacement in this four-cell batch; single paired host seed'],decision_if_supported='Keep M as a provisional improvement in this family; compare to DIN before selecting. Plan constant-gain attribution and paired repetitions if consequential.',decision_if_not_supported='Retain DIN; reject this implementation, preserving normalized controls. Consider a subsequent discriminating full-value bypass or representation control rather than concluding all intensity mechanisms fail.'),\n dict(parent_ref='g1-r0000-exchange_q0_w1',intervention='M x Q factorial: (M1Q1-M0Q1)-(M1Q0-M0Q0)',control='mass_m1_q0 and mass_m0_q0 use first_query for the second read; both still pass first-read fields to mixer and writer',held_fixed=fixed,remaining_confounds=['Both reads receive the M intervention; which round matters is not isolated','Q0 retains indirect feedback, so this tests the additional query path only','AUC is nonlinear; interaction is a descriptive metric contrast and requires repetitions'],decision_if_supported='Provisionally retain the refreshed-query configuration and test repetition plus round-specific or constant-gain replacements before claiming feedback-specific support.',decision_if_not_supported='Do not claim cooperative query/intensity mechanism; retain any simpler main effect only if it improves validation quality or measured cost. Avoid interpreting one negative interaction as universal refutation.'),\n dict(parent_ref='baseline-din',intervention='Best validation cell in the new four-cell suite',control='baseline-din; contextual comparison to all four unsuccessful g1-r0000-exchange cells',held_fixed=['Frozen full data/protocol and selection score'],remaining_confounds=['Architecture and dense capacity differ from DIN','Historical exchange cells lack count scalar; no new exact DIN repetition in this batch'],decision_if_supported='Record provisional performance separately from mechanism support; schedule nearest-control repetitions if resources remain.',decision_if_not_supported='Keep baseline-din as incumbent and faithfully retain all unsuccessful trajectories; do not relabel a within-family rescue as an overall improvement.')\n],\n'cost_plan':{\n 'estimate_ref':'g1-r0000-exchange_q1_w1=339.435s wall,305.407s train,3.2844GB peak; full previous exchange range338.85..345.34s. Frozen estimated_unit_seconds481.348, trial_cap_seconds1203.369, remaining169037.164s at context resolution. New modules add512 dense parameters (expected dense520900,total32314116) and count reductions/scaling; confirm on host. No quadratic sequence attention is added.',\n 'all_variants_counted':True,\n 'attribution_reserve':'Count all4 cells, failed checks and retries. Nominal suite allowance4*481.348=1925.392s, worst per-trial cap allowance4*1203.369=4813.476s. Hold at least6000s for later constant-gain/round-specific replacements and paired repeats; do not request automatic duplicate execution after uncertain state.',\n 'assessment_reserve':'Reserve at least6000s for necessary validation repeats, suite freeze and authorized final assessment. This propose phase requests no holdout execution; final candidate/control/checkpoint/source/config/seed/command hashes must be frozen before any separately authorized assessment. No final-suite selection has happened.',\n 'stop_rule':'Do not train or install in the coding jail. Submit four standalone modules to the host under the frozen protocol. Stop if hard remaining budget cannot cover a complete next unit plus reserves, a trial reaches1203.369s, integrity fails or the user stops. If static/host checks fail, record failure and repair only within remaining budget; never raise limits. Null/negative outcomes are valid and do not imply scientific success.'\n}}\nassess=[]\nfor kid,decision,why,change,diff,falsifier in [\n ('unirank-method-est','used','The prior EST-inspired repeated retrieval family executes correctly but every cell trails DIN. It remains a useful controlled structure, not locally validated evidence of EST effectiveness.','Retain two strict-masked shared-projection reads; cross count-dependent magnitude with refreshed second queries.','No EST feature-specific FFNs or token-specific Q/output projections; inherited field-conditioned write. Original-paper novelty unverified.','No M gain against equal-capacity normalized+count controls, or no M x Q interaction.'),\n ('unirank-method-infnet','used','Inspected benchmark affine aggregation/broadcast is inherited through the existing writer; previous positive write contrasts are single-seed support within a losing family.','Keep the shared field-mean-conditioned affine event writer enabled identically in all cells.','No task-specific hubs/action-mask routing; strict score masks. This batch does not re-estimate the value of writing.','A new gain cannot be attributed to INFNet broadcasting here; future matched write controls could remove it.'),\n ('unirank-method-onetrans','considered','Relevant iterative exchange precedent, but full original primary detail is unavailable. Full attention and sequence reduction add confounds to this diagnostic.','None of its pyramid reduction or mixed FFNs adopted.','No full joint event-event attention or progressive sequence reduction; no novelty relative to original method claimed.','A later matched structure could outperform this family; current outcomes do not refute OneTrans.'),\n ('unirank-method-unimixer','considered','Flattening addresses compression but conflates projection capacity/position sensitivity with the normalization uncertainty. The present batch isolates a cheaper uncertainty first.','No flattening tokenizer or paired streams adopted.','Keep visible events across two rounds; no flattened-history replacement.','If normalized/mass variants all fail, a matched raw-value/flattening control may become consequential; no local UniMixer claim.'),\n ('unirank-method-zenith','rejected','Prior knowledge-usage record was reviewed. No local train-frequency diagnostics justify identifier-capacity changes and they would confound the current test.','None; sparse widths stay16.','No identifier capacity expansion.','Future authorized frequency diagnostics could justify revisiting this choice; no claim of Zenith ineffectiveness.')]:\n assess.append(dict(knowledge_id=kid,decision=decision,rationale=why,transformed_mechanism=change,variant_names=[v['name'] for v in variants] if decision=='used' else [],nearest_work_difference=diff,falsifier=falsifier))\np=dict(study=study,parent_trial='g1-r0000-exchange_q1_w1',variants=variants,knowledge_assessments=assess)\nPath('proposal.json').write_text(json.dumps(p,indent=2)+'\\\\n')\nprint('Wrote proposal.json with four variants and complete prospective study.')\nPY\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
